The [[Lore:Forgotten Vale|Forgotten Vale]] is massive and sprawling secluded ice-encrusted land dotted with the remains of [[Lore:Snow Elf|Snow Elf]] architecture.{{Ref|name=TESVSPOGG|{{Cite Book|The Elder Scrolls V: Skyrim: Prima Official Game Guide|ns_base=BK}}}} Located in the [[Lore:Druadach Mountains|Druadach Mountains]], it is viewed on maps as being within the borders of [[Lore:High Rock|High Rock]] and bordering northwestern [[Lore:Skyrim|Skyrim]]'s Haafingar area.{{ref|name=SRMap|[[:File:SR-map-Skyrim.jpg|Skyrim Map]] — [[Lore:Natalia Dravarol|Nataly Dravarol]]}}{{ref|name=ESODaughter|[[ON:Dragonhome|Dragonhome]] [[Online:Loading Screens|loading screen]] in [[ESO:Greymoor|ESO]]}} It is a glacial valley, with icy crevices, forests, a river and a large frozen lake. Its seclusion from the rest of [[Lore:Tamriel|Tamriel]] has resulted in unique forms of bioluminescent flora and fauna, seemingly adapted for subterranean dwelling.{{ref|name=DG|Events of ''[[Skyrim:Skyrim|Skyrim]]: [[Skyrim:Dawnguard|Dawnguard]]''}}

The vale is difficult to reach, requiring the navigation through the Darkfall Cave systems to enter from the outside world. It was chosen by the ancient [[Lore:Snow Elf|Snow Elves]] as the site of the [[Lore:Chantry of Auri-El|Chantry of Auri-El]], the civilization's center of worship of [[Lore:Auri-El|Auri-El]]. The elves built a large sanctum into the mountains, overlooking the valley, as well as five [[Lore:Wayshrines|Wayshrines]] of Auri-El. Magical teleportation in the form of portals were used to navigate and link the area. In order to reach enlightenment and "become one with Auri-El",{{Ref|name=TESVSPOGG}} initiates of the Chantry made a pilgrimage to each of the five Wayshrines, navigating the treacherous vale with a ewer of water to gain access to the temple's inner sanctum. Due to the Chantry's isolation, it remained unaffected by the invasion of the [[Lore:Nord|Nords]], though the Falmer somehow spread to the vale and overwhelmed the Chantry by their sheer numbers, wiping out the final bastion of Snow Elves.{{ref|name=DGGelebor|[[Skyrim:Knight-Paladin Gelebor|Knight-Paladin Gelebor]]'s dialogue in ''[[Skyrim:Skyrim|Skyrim]]: [[Skyrim:Dawnguard|Dawnguard]]''}}<noinclude>

{{NewLine}}
==Ecosystem==
In the centuries of seclusion from the rest of [[Lore:Tamriel|Tamriel]] has resulted in unique forms of bioluminescent flora and fauna, seemingly adapted for subterranean dwelling. Its animals have grown to be very different than those in Skyrim, home to unique species of [[Lore:Vale Sabre Cat|sabre cat]] and [[Lore:Vale Deer|deer]], though despite their appearance, these creatures have no special resistances or weaknesses.{{Ref|name=TESVSPOGG}} They are called Vale animals, named after a now-lost flora-filled cavern in Skyrim.{{ref|name=Orchidfall|[[Online:Orchidfall Vale Fawn|Orchidfall Vale Fawn]] pet description in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}} [[Lore:Elk|Hailcinder Vale Elk]] have a chosen diet of glowing flora and fungi.{{ref|name=ESOHailcinderValeElk|[[Online:Hailcinder Vale Elk|Hailcinder Vale Elk]] mount description}} The rare and mysterious [[Lore:Shellbug|shellbugs]] have only been documented as being found here, with the more common [[Lore:Frost Troll|frost troll]]s making their homes in dens through the valley, and the insectoid [[Lore:Chaurus|chaurus]] living among their [[Lore:Falmer|Falmer]] handlers.{{ref|name=DG|Events of ''[[Skyrim:Skyrim|Skyrim]]: [[Skyrim:Dawnguard|Dawnguard]]''}} Deep within the Forgotten Vale, some creatures have been transformed into living ice with all the same attributes of their standard counterparts, with the added immunity to frost/weakness to fire and shattering when killed.{{Ref|name=TESVSPOGG}}{{ref|name=DG}} 

The only sentient species permanently residing here are the Snow Elves, who were once more common before their slaughter by the Falmer.{{ref|name=DGGelebor}} The rare [[Lore:Frost Giant|Frost Giants]], a bestial but intelligent species, also have a population spread across the valley dwelling in shallow caves. The Falmer made their home in various parts of the region, setting up a number of villages.{{ref|name=DG}} The Vale was once home to revered twin [[Lore:Dragon|dragons]], {{Lore Link|Voslaarum}} and {{Lore Link|Naaslaarum}}, who lived beneath Frozen Lake. They were most likely killed at some point and resurrected by [[Lore:Alduin|Alduin]] upon his return,{{ref|Based on the dragons not being present before the [[Skyrim:Dragon Rising|Dragon Rising]] quest}} although it is possible that they survived into modernity.

Bar a few rare cases, the [[Lore:Gleamblossom|Gleamblossom]] flower and [[Lore:Poison Bloom|Poison Bloom]] plant are unique to the region.{{ref|name=DG}} There are also strange plant-like cave worms that begin to retract when approached, hiding their bioluminescent light.{{Ref|name=TheCW|[[Skyrim:Passive Creatures#Cave Worm|Cave Worms]] in ''[[SR:Skyrim|Skyrim]]''}}{{Ref|name=TESVSPOGG}} Many glowing crystals are also found throughout the caves.

